ei from 1912. It depicts two children grappling with a fish. The fine workmanship of the fishing net is remarkable."],["Fountain of King Matthias","sight",47.49611,19.03909,"I, Hunyadi Court","","","","","r","This spectacular fountain shows a group of hunters led by King Matthias Corvinus together with hounds, a killed deer, Galeotto Marzio with a hawk, and Ilonka Szép with a doe. This group of people stands between fallen rocks with water…"],["Lion's Gate","sight",47.49578,19.03934,"I, Lion's Court","","","","","r","Two pairs of lions guard the monumental gate leading into Lion's Court. The four statues are the works of János Fadrusz from 1901. The animals standing on the outer side of the gate are menacing, while the inner ones are calm and…"],["Royal Guard","sight",47.49607,19.0386,"I, Hunyadi Court","Fri–Sun 11:00–18:00","","","","r","It was built in 1903 according to plans of Alajos Hauszmann. It was hit by a bomb in World War II, and was demolished in 1971. It was rebuilt between 2017–2021. There is an exhibition about history of the Royal Guard."],["Royal Riding Hall","sight",47.49592,19.03806,"I, Lovarda utca","","","","","r","The Neo-Baroque riding hall was built between 1901 and 1903 in parallel with the construction of the Royal Palace. It was hit by a bomb in World War II, and was demolished in 1954. Rebuilt between 2017–2020. It's used as an event venue."],["Horse Brainer Statue","sight",47.49574,19.03838,"I, Horse Brainer Court","","","","","r","The statue of the Hortobágy horseherd taming a wild horse used to stand in front of the Royal Riding Hall. It is the work of György Vastagh from 1901. The statue was displayed in the Exposition Universelle in Paris (1900). The damaged…"],["The Hauszmann Story exhibition","sight",47.49675,19.03844,"I, Szent György tér 2","Tue–Sun 10:00–18:00","","","","r","The exhibition commemorates the life and the greatest work of the architect Alajos Hauszmann."],["Sándor Palace","sight",47.498,19.03784,"I, Szent György tér 1","Only from outside","","","","r","Built between 1803–1806 in Neoclassical style according to plans of Mihály Pollack and Johann Aman architects as the home of the Sándor family. In 1867, following the idea of Prime Minister Gyula Andrássy, the Hungarian state first…"],["Carmelite Monastery, Castle Theatre","sight",47.49864,19.0375,"I, Színház utca 1","Only from outside","","","","r","The Baroque monastery was built in 1736 by the Carmelite order on the former site of a mosque that was destroyed in 1686 during the siege that liberated Buda from Ottoman occupation. The order received the real estate in 1693 and…"],["Remains of Archduke Joseph's Palace","sight",47.49756,19.03674,"I, Szent György tér 4","","","","","r","Built between 1787–1789 and was significantly remodeled in 1902. The classicist Teleki Palace, completed in 1789, became the property of Archduke Joseph Karl in 1892, who transformed it in Historicizing style. It was badly damaged…"],["Homeland Defence Headquarter","sight",47.49884,19.03663,"I, Dísz tér 17","","","","","r","Built between 1895 and 1897 based on the plans of Mór Kallina. The Neo-Renaissance style, four-story, large-domed building suffered severe damage during World War II. After the war, the damaged dome and upper floors were demolished…"],["Dwelling Houses on Parade Square","sight",47.49925,19.03542,"I, Dísz tér, Tárnok utca","","","","","r","Parade Square is a north to south elongated area, bordered by one- and two-storey hundred years old houses. Major houses of the square: Dísz tér 3: The two-storey building which the back facade oriented towards the Danube, the main…"],["De la Motte–Beer Palace","sight",47.49906,19.03568,"I, Dísz tér 15","Tue–Sun 10:00–18:00","","","","r","One-storey Baroque building. An arcaded corridor runs along the courtyard side, and the upstairs rooms are decorated with frescoes in good condition. In 1760 it became the property of the de la Motte family, who expanded it and made it…"],["Homeland Defence Memorial","sight",47.49955,19.0352,"I, Dísz tér","","","","","r","Made by György Zala in 1893. The statue commemorating the War of Liberation of 1848–1849. The revolution in the Kingdom of Hungary grew into a war for independence from the Austrian Empire, ruled by the Habsburg dynasty."],["Statue of Artúr Görgey","sight",47.49834,19.03554,"I, Tóth Árpád sétány","","","","","r","The original sculpture was made by György Vastagh and erected in 1935, the current one is a copy made by László Marton, which was placed here in 1998."],["House of Houdini","activity",47.49938,19.035,"I, Dísz tér 11","10:00–19:00","","","","r","Houdini memorial house. There is a showroom and an exhibition with authentic Houdini memorabilia."],["Korona Cafe","bar",47.49874,19.03606,"I, Dísz tér 16","10:00–18:00","","","","r","Cafe, confectionery and breakfast."],["Vár Bistro","bar",47.49975,19.03497,"I, Dísz tér 8","19:00–20:00","","","","r","Cafe, confectionery and breakfast."],["Hegyvidék Region History Collection","sight",47.49281,19.02017,"Beethoven utca 1/b","Tue Thu Fri 10:00-18:00","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Lutheran Church of Buda Mountain","sight",47.49876,19.02102,"XII. Kékgolyó u. 17.","","","","","r","Lutheran church."],["Palace MOM PARK Cinema Complex","activity",47.49053,19.02351,"XII. Alkotás utca","","","","","r","Which is the \"Original language movie\" in Budapest, so you can watch all the foreign movies here with subtitles too. Check Palace’s web site for programme and booking."],["MOM Sports Swimming Pool and Sports Centre","activity",47.49007,19.02263,"XII. Csörsz u. 14-16","Daily 06:00-22:00","","","","r","Rentals: Sports hall (size: 1.600m²), ballet room (110m²), Artificial grass football field (40m x 20m). email about rental=peter.horvath@momsport.hu Pools: Spa pools for wellness great relaxation for the 16-person hot tub, two Finnish…"],["Budapest Congress Center","activity",47.48852,19.02233,"XII. Jagelló út 1-3","","","","","r","The largest, most modern c